From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: complete FE recovery and preserve mux ownership

Match the WiFi stop and N9-normal recovery phases, wait for an explicitly
registered NPU client, and leave DMA untouched after missing quiesce ACKs.
Bound all waits and make them cancelable before device teardown. A failed
stop-to-reset fallback must resume WiFi with RESET_DONE, not START_TRAFFIC.

Track each MAC's successful open so a failed mux/reset reopen cannot close
another port's DMA reference. Retry failed mux opens and exclude switches
during FE recovery. Keep diagnostic readers alive until their nodes drain,
and handle an absent switch mapping without an uninitialized MMIO pointer.
Serialize reset producers against teardown and drain failed probe paths
with HNAT enabled as well. The proprietary HNAT owner remains independent
of the upstream PPE.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>

